- op: discuss  # 5b72
  at: '2026-10-22T15:31:50Z'  # 5b72
  by: agent  # 5b72
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5b72
  clock: 3  # 5b72
  nonce: 5b72  # 5b72
  message: "Fixed in c4d7ba35da (dev). swift_objc's import src is the existing file node (or make_file_id('objc', rel) when none), and its dst is objc:<header>:0-0:header:header, the cpp/objc header convention. Linker ids carry the swift language slot, and the role goes in the name via _ROLE_FOLDS. Live repro on dev ad12089f32: App-Bridging-Header.h (#import \"Legacy.h\", <UIKit/UIKit.h>), Legacy.h/.m, main.swift; hypergumbo run, survey.json. The swift-objc-linker run reports edges_emitted=2. Both merge into the objc analyzer's identical imports edges, possible only because the ids now agree: objc:App-Bridging-Header.h:1-1:file:file -> objc:Legacy.h:0-0:header:external_symbol and -> objc:UIKit/UIKit.h:0-0:header:external_symbol, src and dst both present as nodes. No id anywhere has the old swift_objc language slot (0). Not done: the in-repo Legacy.h import lands on a header placeholder, not on the Legacy.h file node (a resolution question, like WI-modan)."  # 5b72
